 name you give your rescue companion can honor their journey, celebrate their fresh start, and reflect the hope and love that define their new life.\"]}],\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\",\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\",\"$L2d\",\"$L2e\",\"$L2f\",\"$L30\",\"$L31\"]}],\"$L32\",\"$L33\",\"$L34\",\"$L35\",\"$L36\",\"$L37\"]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Names Meaning Hope & New Beginnings\"]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Nova</strong> (new), <strong>Aurora</strong> (dawn), <strong>Dawn</strong>, <strong>Renee</strong> (reborn), <strong>Phoenix</strong> (risen from ashes), <strong>Zera</strong> (new beginning), <strong>Anastasia</strong> (resurrection).\"}}]\n25:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Names Meaning Strength & Survival\"]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"p\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Rocky</strong>, <strong>Survivor</strong>, <strong>Champion</strong>, <strong>Valor</strong>, <strong>Titan</strong>, <strong>Atlas</strong>, <strong>Warrior</strong>. These names honor the resilience of rescued animals.\"}}]\n27:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Names Meaning Lucky & Blessed\"]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Lucky</strong>, <strong>Chance</strong>, <strong>Felix</strong> (lucky), <strong>Clover</strong>, <strong>Fortuna</strong>, <strong>Kismet</strong>, <strong>Destiny</strong>, <strong>Serendipity</strong>.\"}}]\n29:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Names About the Journey\"]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Explore our name generators for \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"32\",{\"href\":\"/animal/arabian-leopard/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Arabian Leopard\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"51\",{\"href\":\"/animal/antechinus/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Antechinus\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"65\",{\"href\":\"/animal/andean-fox/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Andean Fox\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"79\",{\"href\":\"/animal/airedale-terrier/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Airedale Terrier\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"103\",{\"href\":\"/animal/anthias/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Anthias\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" to find the perfect name for your companion.\"]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Journey</strong>, <strong>Quest</strong>, <strong>Roamer</strong>, <strong>Wander</strong>, <strong>Pilgrim</strong>, <strong>Foundling</strong>, <strong>Discovery</strong>, <strong>Homeward</strong>.\"}}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Naming Rescue Dogs: Special Considerations\"]}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Rescue dogs often arrive with unknown histories, making the naming process both more challenging and more meaningful. Unlike puppies from breeders, rescue dogs may have experienced trauma, neglect, or multiple rehomings. A new name represents a clean break from whatever came before. When choosing a name for your rescue \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"321\",{\"href\":\"/animal/marmoset/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Marmoset\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", prioritize positive associations — avoid names that sound like commands ('Kit' sounds like 'sit,' 'Bo' sounds like 'no'). Observe your dog's personality for at least 3-5 days before deciding, as shelter stress can mask their true character.\"]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Naming Rescue Cats: Finding Their Voice\"]}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Cats from shelters and rescues may be shy, independent, or instantly affectionate — let their emerging personality guide your name choice. For a cat who hides at first but gradually blooms, consider names about emergence: Dawn, Bloom, Bud, Spring. For a cat who claims your lap immediately, names about confidence: Duchess, King, Boss, Queenie. For names organized by breed and personality type, explore our \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"408\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Cat\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" name generator with specialized categories for every feline friend.\"]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"The Emotional Power of Rescue Names\"]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Many adopters report that choosing the right name for their rescue animal was a defining moment in their relationship. 'When I named him Chance,' says David, who adopted a three-legged \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"185\",{\"href\":\"/animal/green-iguana/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Green Iguana\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", 'I wasn't just giving him a name — I was making a promise. Every time I call him, I'm reminded of the second chance we both got.' This emotional resonance is unique to rescue naming and makes the process profoundly different from naming a pet from a breeder or store.\"]}]\n32:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should I rename a rescue animal?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes! Most rescue animals adapt quickly to new names. A fresh name can be part of their fresh start and helps leave past trauma behind.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What if the shelter already named them?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Shelter names are usually temporary. Feel free to choose your own — most animals respond to tone and love more than syllables.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I help a rescue animal learn their new name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Use treats, positive reinforcement, and repetition. Say their name with warmth and reward them when they look at you. Most learn within 1-2 weeks.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I know if my rescue pet likes their new name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Watch for positive reactions: ear perk, tail wag, head turn, or coming toward you. Use the name consistently with treats and affection for 5-7 days. If your pet consistently responds positively, the name is working. If they ignore it or seem stressed, try a different name — some sounds may remind them of negative past experiences.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should I keep the shelter name if my pet responds to it?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"If your pet responds well to their shelter name and it has no negative connotations for you, keeping it is the easiest path. However, many adopters prefer a fresh start. If you change it, choose something phonetically similar (same first letter or syllable count) to ease the transition. The most important factor is your pet's comfort with the name.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are some powerful names for pets who survived trauma?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Names symbolizing resilience and recovery are especially meaningful: Phoenix (rebirth), Valor (courage), Hope, Chance, Journey, Survivor, Rocky (strength), Karma, Destiny, and Grace. These names honor your pet's past while celebrating their future. Many adopters also choose names meaning 'lucky' — Felix, Clover, Fortune, Asher (blessed), and Chance.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are there special naming considerations for senior rescue animals?\"}],\"$L38\"]}]]}]]}]\n33:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"dog\",{\"href\":\"/animal/dog/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐕\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Dog\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"cat\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐱\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Cat\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"tibetan-terrier\",{\"href\":\"/animal/tibetan-terrier/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐕\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Tibetan Terrier\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"hoopoe\",{\"href\":\"/animal/hoopoe/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"ch